[ti:Why DeepEP and MXFP8 Make DeepSeek-V3 Training 41% Faster]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: What if you could train a 671B-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model 41% faster, using open-source PyTorch tools?
[00:00.00]Ava：如果用开源 PyTorch 工具，能把一个 671B 参数的专家混合模型训练速度提高 41%，会怎样？
[00:09.54]That’s the result we’re unpacking today.
[00:09.54]这就是我们今天要聊的成果。
[00:13.36]Brian: And the interesting part is that the gain comes from two different places: MXFP8 speeds up matrix multiplication, while DeepEP speeds up expert communication.
[00:13.36]Brian：有意思的是，提速来自两个方面：MXFP8 加快矩阵乘法，DeepEP 加快专家间通信。
[00:26.79]Together, they reached 918 tokens per second on 256 NVIDIA B200 GPUs.
[00:26.79]两者结合后，在 256 块 NVIDIA B200 GPU 上达到了每秒 918 个 token。
[00:33.00]Ava: Let’s start with the setup. This was a joint PyTorch and Nebius experiment, right?
[00:33.00]Ava：先说实验配置。这是 PyTorch 和 Nebius 联合做的实验，对吧？
[00:38.90]Brian: Right. They used TorchTitan as the pre-training framework on a Nebius Cloud cluster.
[00:38.90]Brian：对。他们在 Nebius Cloud 集群上，用 TorchTitan 作为预训练框架。
[00:46.45]The cluster had 32 nodes, eight B200 GPUs per node, so 256 GPUs in total.
[00:46.45]集群有 32 个节点，每个节点 8 块 B200 GPU，总共 256 块。
[00:53.36]Ava: And the model was DeepSeek-V3, with both a 671B version and a 16B MoE version.
[00:53.36]Ava：模型是 DeepSeek-V3，分别用了 671B 版本和 16B MoE 版本。
[01:01.92]Brian: Exactly. The 671B experiment measured throughput.
[01:01.92]Brian：没错。671B 实验测的是吞吐量。
[01:06.41]The 16B experiment checked whether MXFP8 changes training convergence.
[01:06.41]16B 实验检验 MXFP8 是否影响训练收敛。
[01:13.16]Ava: Why focus on Mixture-of-Experts models? What makes them difficult to train?
[01:13.16]Ava：为什么聚焦专家混合模型？它们难训在哪里？
[01:19.08]Brian: They have two major costs. First, the experts do a lot of matrix multiplication.
[01:19.08]Brian：主要有两项开销。首先，专家需要做大量矩阵乘法。
[01:25.18]Second, every layer needs two all-to-all exchanges: one to dispatch tokens to experts, and another to combine the results.
[01:25.18]其次，每一层都要进行两次全对全通信：一次把 token 分发给专家，一次汇总结果。
[01:34.84]Ava: So computation and communication can both become bottlenecks.
[01:34.84]Ava：所以计算和通信都可能成为瓶颈。
[01:39.99]Brian: Yes. And the communication pattern is especially awkward.
[01:39.99]Brian：对。而且它的通信模式尤其棘手。
[01:44.33]The router decides dynamically which tokens go to which experts.
[01:44.33]路由器会动态决定把哪些 token 送给哪些专家。
[01:49.21]That means the transfer sizes and destinations change at every step.
[01:49.21]这意味着每一步的传输量和目标位置都会变化。
[01:54.74]Ava: Which is a bad match for a generic all-to-all operation designed around fixed transfers.
[01:54.74]Ava：这就不太适合按固定传输设计的通用全对全操作。
[02:00.90]Brian: That’s the idea.
[02:00.90]Brian：正是如此。
[02:02.31]As expert parallelism, or EP, grows, this communication cost gets worse.
[02:02.31]随着专家并行，也就是 EP，的规模扩大，通信开销会更高。
[02:08.67]In the 671B run, EP was 32 across 32 nodes, so inter-node traffic mattered a lot.
[02:08.67]671B 实验在 32 个节点上采用 EP=32，因此跨节点流量影响很大。
[02:16.18]Ava: Okay. Let’s talk about the first optimization: MXFP8. What does the name mean?
[02:16.18]Ava：好。先聊第一项优化：MXFP8。这个名字是什么意思？
[02:23.39]Brian: MXFP8 means Microscaling FP8.
[02:23.39]Brian：MXFP8 是微缩放 FP8。
[02:26.03]It’s a low-precision format defined by the OCP Microscaling Specification.
[02:26.03]它是 OCP 微缩放规范定义的一种低精度格式。
[02:32.75]Standard float8 often uses one scale factor per tensor or per row.
[02:32.75]标准 float8 通常每个张量或每一行共用一个缩放因子。
[02:38.75]MXFP8 uses a shared exponent, called an E8M0 scale, for every block of 32 elements.
[02:38.75]MXFP8 则每 32 个元素共用一个指数，称为 E8M0 缩放值。
[02:46.64]Ava: So the scaling is more local.
[02:46.64]Ava：也就是说，缩放范围更局部。
[02:49.55]Brian: Right.
[02:49.55]Brian：对。
[02:50.04]That finer-grained scaling helps preserve numerical fidelity while still using FP8 tensor cores.
[02:50.04]这种更细粒度的缩放有助于保持数值精度，同时仍能使用 FP8 张量核心。
[02:57.85]NVIDIA Blackwell supports MXFP8 natively through its tcgen05.
[02:57.85]NVIDIA Blackwell 通过 tcgen05.
[03:02.82]mma tensor core instructions.
[03:02.82]mma 张量核心指令原生支持 MXFP8。
[03:05.53]Ava: That’s why B200 is a natural target. There’s no emulation overhead for MXFP8 GEMMs.
[03:05.53]Ava：所以 B200 很适合跑它。MXFP8 GEMM 不需要模拟，因而没有这方面的开销。
[03:13.77]Brian: Yes. Blackwell can provide up to two times the peak TFLOPS of BF16 for eligible GEMMs.
[03:13.77]Brian：对。对于适用的 GEMM，Blackwell 的峰值 TFLOPS 最高可达 BF16 的两倍。
[03:19.94]But the article measures end-to-end training, so the real speedup depends on overhead and on which operations are eligible.
[03:19.94]但文章测的是端到端训练，实际提速取决于额外开销，以及哪些操作能用 MXFP8。
[03:29.10]Ava: How did TorchTitan apply it?
[03:29.10]Ava：TorchTitan 是怎么用上它的？
[03:31.63]Brian: Through TorchAO.
[03:31.63]Brian：通过 TorchAO。
[03:32.87]For linear layers, TorchAO dynamically quantizes inputs to MXFP8 for the forward output, input gradient, and weight gradient GEMMs.
[03:32.87]在线性层中，TorchAO 会为前向输出、输入梯度和权重梯度这三类 GEMM，将输入动态量化为 MXFP8。
[03:42.99]The results accumulate back to BF16.
[03:42.99]计算结果则累加为 BF16。
[03:46.12]Ava: And for the experts?
[03:46.12]Ava：专家层呢？
[03:48.08]Brian: For routed experts, it converts torch grouped matrix multiplication operations to a TorchAO grouped GEMM function.
[03:48.08]Brian：对于路由专家，它把 torch 的分组矩阵乘法操作转换为 TorchAO 的分组 GEMM 函数。
[03:56.88]The same three GEMMs use dynamically quantized MXFP8 inputs.
[03:56.88]这三类 GEMM 同样使用动态量化为 MXFP8 的输入。
[04:01.87]Ava: The article says grouped GEMMs dominate MoE expert layers.
[04:01.87]Ava：文章说，分组 GEMM 是 MoE 专家层的主要开销。
[04:06.32]Brian: Exactly. The recipe quantizes inputs immediately before each grouped GEMM.
[04:06.32]Brian：没错。这套方案会在每次分组 GEMM 前立即量化输入。
[04:11.69]When the GEMM dimensions are large, the compute cost grows faster than the quantization cost, so the overhead becomes relatively small.
[04:11.69]GEMM 维度较大时，计算量比量化开销增长得更快，所以量化的相对开销会变小。
[04:21.84]Ava: But for small dimensions, quantization can cancel the benefit.
[04:21.84]Ava：但维度较小时，量化开销可能抵消收益。
[04:26.44]Brian: Yes. The article is clear about that limitation.
[04:26.44]Brian：对。文章明确指出了这个局限。
[04:30.01]In smaller MoE models, the quantization overhead can match or exceed the MXFP8 speedup, leading to neutral or even negative performance.
[04:30.01]在较小的 MoE 模型中，量化开销可能等于甚至超过 MXFP8 带来的提速，最终性能持平，甚至下降。
[04:40.47]Ava: Now DeepEP sounds like a very different kind of optimization.
[04:40.47]Ava：DeepEP 听起来是另一种优化。
[04:45.52]Brian: It is.
[04:45.52]Brian：是的。
[04:45.97]DeepEP is a GPU communication library developed by DeepSeek specifically for MoE expert-parallel dispatch and combine operations.
[04:45.97]DeepEP 是 DeepSeek 专为 MoE 专家并行中的 token 分发和结果汇总开发的 GPU 通信库。
[04:56.05]Ava: What does it change compared with standard all-to-all?
[04:56.05]Ava：与标准的全对全通信相比，它改变了什么？
[04:59.83]Brian: It uses purpose-built NVLink and RDMA kernels.
[04:59.83]Brian：它使用专门设计的 NVLink 和 RDMA 内核。
[05:03.79]Inside a node, data moves over high-bandwidth NVLink.
[05:03.79]节点内，数据通过高带宽 NVLink 传输。
[05:08.35]Between nodes, it uses RDMA over InfiniBand.
[05:08.35]节点间，则通过 InfiniBand 使用 RDMA。
[05:12.14]This hierarchical path matches the hardware’s bandwidth differences.
[05:12.14]这种分层传输方式适应了硬件带宽的差异。
[05:18.35]Ava: The article mentions around 900 gigabytes per second for intra-node NVLink.
[05:18.35]Ava：文章提到，节点内 NVLink 的带宽约为每秒 900 GB。
[05:24.58]Brian: Yes, that’s the approximate figure given for the setup.
[05:24.58]Brian：对，这是该配置给出的近似值。
[05:28.85]DeepEP also uses NVSHMEM, which provides a Partitioned Global Address Space.
[05:28.85]DeepEP 还使用 NVSHMEM，它提供分区全局地址空间。
[05:34.74]Each GPU can map a symmetric memory region that peers can address.
[05:34.74]每个 GPU 都能映射一块其他 GPU 可寻址的对称内存区域。
[05:40.22]Ava: And with InfiniBand GPUDirect Async, the GPU can drive network operations directly from CUDA kernels.
[05:40.22]Ava：借助 InfiniBand GPUDirect Async，GPU 还能直接从 CUDA 内核发起网络操作。
[05:48.80]Brian: Right. That removes CPU involvement, which is useful for small, dynamic transfers.
[05:48.80]Brian：没错。这省去了 CPU 的参与，尤其适合小规模、动态的数据传输。
[05:54.93]DeepEP also fuses metadata such as token embeddings, expert indices, and routing weights into one communication operation.
[05:54.93]DeepEP 还将词元嵌入、专家索引和路由权重等信息合并到一次通信操作中。
[06:04.41]Ava: Fewer launches and fewer synchronization points.
[06:04.41]Ava：这样启动次数和同步点都更少。
[06:08.41]Brian: Exactly.
[06:08.41]Brian：正是如此。
[06:08.99]It can also be configured to use a chosen number of streaming multiprocessors, leaving the remaining SMs available for overlapping computation.
[06:08.99]它还可以配置为只使用指定数量的流式多处理器，让剩余的 SM 用于并行计算。
[06:19.75]Ava: Before the results, tell me about the actual 671B training configuration.
[06:19.75]Ava：讲结果之前，先说说 671B 模型的实际训练配置。
[06:26.15]Brian: The sequence length was 8192, with a local batch size of 64.
[06:26.15]Brian：序列长度为 8192，本地批量大小为 64。
[06:32.21]Tensor Parallel, or TP, was 2. Pipeline Parallel, PP, was 2. Data Parallel, DP, was 1.
[06:32.21]张量并行 TP 为 2，流水线并行 PP 为 2，数据并行 DP 为 1。
[06:40.89]Expert Parallel was 32, and Expert Tensor Parallel was 1.
[06:40.89]专家并行 EP 为 32，专家张量并行为 1。
[06:47.00]Ava: They also used full activation checkpointing and torch. compile for the model and loss.
[06:47.00]Ava：他们还使用了完整激活检查点，并用 torch.compile 编译模型和损失函数。
[06:53.68]Brian: Correct.
[06:53.68]Brian：没错。
[06:54.28]The learning rate was one times ten to the minus four, with 2,000 warmup steps, and the dataset was C4.
[06:54.28]学习率为 1×10⁻⁴，预热 2,000 步，数据集为 C4。
[07:02.36]Ava: What were the three configurations?
[07:02.36]Ava：三种配置分别是什么？
[07:05.28]Brian: First, BF16 with standard expert parallel communication.
[07:05.28]Brian：第一种是 BF16，使用标准的专家并行通信。
[07:10.98]That was the baseline at 651 tokens per second. Second, BF16 with DeepEP.
[07:10.98]这是基线，每秒处理 651 个词元。第二种是 BF16 加 DeepEP。
[07:18.42]Third, MXFP8 on all grouped GEMMs together with DeepEP.
[07:18.42]第三种是所有分组 GEMM 都使用 MXFP8，并搭配 DeepEP。
[07:24.37]Ava: And DeepEP alone reached 859 tokens per second.
[07:24.37]Ava：单用 DeepEP 就达到了每秒 859 个词元。
[07:29.55]Brian: Yes. That’s a 32% improvement over the 651-token baseline.
[07:29.55]Brian：对，比每秒 651 个词元的基线提升了 32%。
[07:35.14]It was the single largest individual gain.
[07:35.14]这是单项优化中最大的提升。
[07:39.54]Ava: So communication was the dominant bottleneck at that scale.
[07:39.54]Ava：所以在这个规模下，通信是主要瓶颈。
[07:44.21]Brian: That’s the interpretation in the article.
[07:44.21]Brian：文章是这样解读的。
[07:47.50]With EP equal to 32 across 32 nodes, inter-node all-to-all was a major part of step time.
[07:47.50]EP 为 32、跨越 32 个节点时，节点间全对全通信占了单步训练时间的很大一部分。
[07:54.63]DeepEP’s NVLink and RDMA forwarding reduced that cost substantially.
[07:54.63]DeepEP 通过 NVLink 和 RDMA 转发，大幅降低了这部分开销。
[08:00.43]Ava: Then adding MXFP8 grouped GEMMs pushed throughput to 918 tokens per second, for a total gain of 41%.
[08:00.43]Ava：再加上 MXFP8 分组 GEMM，吞吐量达到每秒 918 个词元，总提升为 41%。
[08:10.21]Brian: Right. The two optimizations composed well because they target different bottlenecks.
[08:10.21]Brian：对。两项优化配合得很好，因为它们针对不同的瓶颈。
[08:17.23]DeepEP works on all-to-all communication. MXFP8 works on GEMM computation.
[08:17.23]DeepEP 优化全对全通信，MXFP8 优化 GEMM 计算。
[08:23.69]Ava: The article says the combined result is close to the sum of the individual improvements.
[08:23.69]Ava：文章说，组合后的提升接近两项单独提升之和。
[08:29.68]Brian: Yes, although the exact individual MXFP8-only number isn’t reported in the summary table.
[08:29.68]Brian：是的，不过汇总表没有报告单用 MXFP8 的确切结果。
[08:37.10]What’s reported is the baseline, the DeepEP result, and the combined result.
[08:37.10]表中报告的是基线、使用 DeepEP 的结果，以及组合使用的结果。
[08:43.78]Ava: That’s a useful distinction. We shouldn’t invent a separate MXFP8 speedup.
[08:43.78]Ava：这个区别很重要。我们不能凭空给出 MXFP8 单独带来的加速幅度。
[08:50.18]Brian: Exactly.
[08:50.18]Brian：没错。
[08:50.88]The evidence supports complementarity, not a precise standalone percentage for MXFP8 in this 671B comparison.
[08:50.88]这些数据能说明两项优化互补，却无法得出 MXFP8 在这次 671B 对比中单独提升的准确百分比。
[09:00.82]Ava: Now, speed is only useful if training still behaves correctly.
[09:00.82]Ava：速度提升的前提是训练仍然正常。
[09:05.81]How did they validate that?
[09:05.81]他们是怎么验证的？
[09:08.33]Brian: They used the 16B DeepSeek-V3 MoE model and ran BF16 and MXFP8 experiments for 1,500 training steps.
[09:08.33]Brian：他们用 16B 的 DeepSeek-V3 MoE 模型，分别进行了 1,500 步的 BF16 和 MXFP8 训练实验。
[09:17.44]These runs used standard EP, without DeepEP.
[09:17.44]这些实验使用标准 EP，没有使用 DeepEP。
[09:21.80]Ava: What was different in the 16B setup?
[09:21.80]Ava：16B 的配置有什么不同？
[09:25.32]Brian: The local batch size was 16. TP and PP were both 1, DP was 1, and EP was still 32.
[09:25.32]Brian：本地批量大小为 16。TP 和 PP 都为 1，DP 为 1，EP 仍为 32。
[09:31.91]They used sequence length 8192, full activation checkpointing, torch.
[09:31.91]序列长度为 8192，使用完整激活检查点，并用 torch.
[09:37.46]compile for model and loss, the same learning rate of one times ten to the minus four, 2,000 warmup steps, and the C4 dataset.
[09:37.46]compile 编译模型和损失函数；学习率同为 1×10⁻⁴，预热 2,000 步，数据集为 C4。
[09:47.94]Ava: And the loss curves?
[09:47.94]Ava：损失曲线呢？
[09:49.93]Brian: They were virtually identical.
[09:49.93]Brian：几乎完全一致。
[09:52.24]The article says MXFP8 showed no meaningful divergence from BF16 over that training window.
[09:52.24]文章称，在这段训练期间，MXFP8 与 BF16 没有出现明显偏离。
[09:59.61]Ava: So MXFP8 was equivalent to BF16 for convergence in this experiment.
[09:59.61]Ava：也就是说，在这次实验中，MXFP8 和 BF16 的收敛表现相当。
[10:06.18]Brian: Yes, over 1,500 steps on the 16B model.
[10:06.18]Brian：对，在 16B 模型上训练了 1,500 步。
[10:09.44]That supports the numerical stability of the recipe, while staying within the scope of the test.
[10:09.44]这说明该训练方案在测试范围内具有数值稳定性。
[10:17.81]Ava: Let’s discuss the limitations and what comes next.
[10:17.81]Ava：聊聊局限和下一步吧。
[10:22.26]Brian: The 671B experiment only applied MXFP8 to grouped GEMMs, meaning the routed experts.
[10:22.26]Brian：671B 模型的实验只对分组 GEMM，也就是路由专家，使用了 MXFP8。
[10:29.39]It couldn’t apply MXFP8 to attention and shared-expert linear layers.
[10:29.39]注意力层和共享专家的线性层还无法使用 MXFP8。
[10:35.60]Ava: Why not?
[10:35.60]Ava：为什么？
[10:37.17]Brian: Because torch.
[10:37.17]Brian：因为 torch。
[10:38.30]compile didn’t yet support MXFP8 linear layers when combined with tensor parallelism.
[10:38.30]compile 当时还不支持与张量并行结合使用的 MXFP8 线性层。
[10:45.14]The 671B configuration required TP equal to 2, so those linear layers were excluded.
[10:45.14]671B 模型的配置要求 TP 为 2，因此这些线性层被排除在外。
[10:52.26]Ava: Once TP, torch.
[10:52.26]Ava：等 TP、torch。
[10:53.51]compile, and MXFP8 linear-layer support work together in TorchTitan, throughput may improve further.
[10:53.51]compile 和 MXFP8 线性层支持能在 TorchTitan 中协同工作，吞吐量可能进一步提升。
[11:02.21]Brian: That’s the expected next step described by the authors.
[11:02.21]Brian：这正是作者提出的下一步。
[11:06.17]They also provide open-source recipes and training configurations for reproducibility on a Nebius Cloud B200 cluster.
[11:06.17]他们还公开了训练方案和配置，方便在 Nebius Cloud 的 B200 集群上复现。
[11:14.96]Ava: The infrastructure story is part of the experiment too.
[11:14.96]Ava：基础设施也是这次实验的一部分。
[11:18.81]Nebius used Soperator, which brings Slurm-style scheduling and multi-node behavior to Kubernetes.
[11:18.81]Nebius 使用 Soperator，让 Kubernetes 具备 Slurm 式调度和多节点运行能力。
[11:25.95]Brian: Yes.
[11:25.95]Brian：没错。
[11:26.25]It continuously checked GPU and interconnect health, including NCCL all-reduce benchmarks and GPU XID errors.
[11:26.25]它持续检查 GPU 和互连的健康状况，包括 NCCL all-reduce 基准测试和 GPU XID 错误。
[11:34.62]Nodes below performance thresholds could be drained and replaced automatically.
[11:34.62]性能低于阈值的节点可以自动退出运行并被替换。
[11:41.03]Ava: And resizing was a single command, with new nodes inheriting the runtime environment.
[11:41.03]Ava：扩容也只需一条命令，新节点会继承运行环境。
[11:48.01]Brian: That reduced the operational work around cluster setup, stragglers, and failed jobs, so the team could focus on the training recipe.
[11:48.01]Brian：这减少了集群搭建、慢节点和任务失败带来的运维工作，让团队能专注于训练方案。
[11:57.14]Ava: Let’s close with the three points I’d write down.
[11:57.14]Ava：最后总结我会记下的三点。
[12:01.65]First: for the 671B model, DeepEP was the biggest lever, taking throughput from 651 to 859 tokens per second.
[12:01.65]第一，对 671B 模型来说，DeepEP 的作用最大，将吞吐量从每秒 651 个 token 提升到 859 个。
[12:12.03]Brian: Second: adding MXFP8 grouped GEMMs to DeepEP reached 918 tokens per second, a 41% total gain, because compute and communication optimizations complemented each other.
[12:12.03]Brian：第二，在 DeepEP 基础上加入 MXFP8 分组 GEMM 后，吞吐量达到每秒 918 个 token，总体提升 41%，因为计算和通信优化相互配合。
[12:26.71]Ava: Third: on the 16B model, MXFP8 and BF16 had equivalent loss behavior over 1,500 steps, while broader MXFP8 coverage still depends on TP and torch.
[12:26.71]Ava：第三，在 16B 模型上，MXFP8 和 BF16 训练 1,500 步的损失表现相当；但要将 MXFP8 用于更多层，仍取决于 TP 和 torch。
[12:41.18]compile support.
[12:41.18]compile 的支持。
[12:43.12]Brian: That’s the whole story: faster expert communication, faster eligible GEMMs, and convergence that stayed aligned in the tested window.
[12:43.12]Brian：这就是全部：专家通信更快，适用的 GEMM 更快，而且在测试期间收敛表现保持一致。
